            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0392" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg378"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34522/52: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-13T19:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 14—12:39 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>835. The following telegram has been sent to Panama.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>October 13, 6 p.m. For General Andrews. Galápagos negotiations have been
                        postponed indefinitely. Captains Stone, Symington, and Colonel Montesinos
                        returning to Canal Zone October 14. Repeated to Department.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
